    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Look.</strong> The family solicitor, a damp and nervous halfling. Fogged spectacles, dripping cloak, a satchel (holding the old will) clutched to his chest. Arrives at midnight by the ferry path.</p><p><strong>Wants.</strong> To read the correct will, be paid, and go home to bed.</p><p><strong>Knows.</strong> The old will leaves everything to Edric. Silas told him a new will existed but not its contents. A genuine Ravenmoor will bears Silas's black raven seal, so he can confirm the recovered will on sight.</p><p><strong>Plays as.</strong> Fussy and easily startled, scrupulously honest. Reads whichever valid will is in front of him at midnight.</p><p><strong>Lines.</strong></p><ul><li>“Fennick Barrowdown, solicitor. I'm here to read Lord Ravenmoor's will. Which will, I'm told, is... in question?”</li></ul>",
        "public": ""
      },
